    "title": "FALL3D Volcanic plume dispersion modelling",
    "description": "Workflow of the FALL3D modelling service for volcanic ash dispersion, supporting user-defined what-if scenarios. The scenario type controls the initial eruptive column height, while initial conditions define the initial concentration fields for the simulation, ranging from zero initial concentration (NONE) to using a previous model run (RESTART). Example applications include the 2018 Etna and 2021 La Palma eruptions",
